9.5 Recommendation Scoring System

Build an initial weighted evaluation model:

Component| Weight
Technical analysis| 35%
Fundamental analysis| 25%
Liquidity and volume| 15%
News and disclosures| 15%
Market and sector conditions| 10%
Total| 100%

The model must be configurable.

Calculate each component separately.

Do not allow a high score in one category to hide serious problems in another category.

Introduce mandatory risk gates.

Examples:

- Severe negative official disclosure.
- Extremely weak liquidity.
- Unresolved price data conflict.
- Insufficient historical data.
- Major financial deterioration.
- Trading suspension.
- Unacceptable risk/reward.

These conditions must prevent inappropriate BUY recommendations.

9.6 Confidence Score

